  "body": "### Summary\n\nWanted by LOT-082 and the bug #103: logged out, `forum1.php?…&page=<n>` answers 301 to `liste_sujet-<n>.htm`; the **logged-in** behaviour of both URL forms is not captured (HFR-PROTOCOL §7b B2, unsettled). Read-only requests only.\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: logged-in GET of `forum1.php?…&page=N` and of `liste_sujet-N.htm` for N > 1 on one forum: status, redirect target, page content (anonymized), and whether `liste_sujet-1.htm?page=N` ignores `page`.\n\n### Sources\n\n- docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md §7b B2; bug #103; LOT-041 builder, LOT-082 navigation\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Anonymized captures with status/redirect notes; B2 settled in HFR-PROTOCOL §7b.\n- [ ] Row removed from the Capture backlog; #103 updated with the result.\n\nRules: LOT-001 kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), anonymize every free-text field, independent leak check before any push, never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36), legacy oracle when a parser consumes it, one PR per batch of captures, the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog in `docs/LOTS.md`. Write captures need the operator approval first.",
